=== Sliceable Types ===
--- Range indexer beside an int indexer ---
middle=20;30;40; single=20 last=50
tail=40;50; all=10;20;30;40;50;
--- Slice(int, int) over every bound form ---
  Slice(1, 2)
tape[1+2]
  Slice(0, 2)
tape[0+2]
  read Count
  Slice(4, 2)
tape[4+2]
  read Count
  Slice(0, 6)
tape[0+6]
  read Count
  Slice(2, 3)
tape[2+3]
  read Count
  Slice(1, 4)
tape[1+4]
  Slice(2, 0)
tape[2+0]
  read Count
  Slice(2, 2)
tape[2+2]
--- Receiver, bounds and Slice each run once, in order ---
  make receiver
  bound 1
  bound 4
  Slice(1, 3)
tape[1+3]
  make receiver
  bound 1
  bound 1
  read Count
  Slice(1, 4)
tape[1+4]
--- A generic owner's result is closed by the receiver ---
right left left
--- An inherited Range indexer reads through its constructed base ---
BADGE
--- List patterns slice through the same members ---
  read Count
  Slice(1, 4)
inner=tape[1+4]
head=10 body=20;30;40; end=50
  read Count
  Slice(2, 4)
after=tape[2+4]
  read Count
bare slice, no Slice call
--- CLR sequences slice through their own Slice ---
memory=2 segment=3
=== Sliceable Types Done ===
